### Local CRM API through the Nginx proxy (Compose host port 8080).
### For direct CRM access, change baseUrl to http://localhost:8181/api.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@application = REPLACE_WITH_CONFIGURED_APPLICATION
@email = REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN_EMAIL
@password = REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN_PASSWORD
@token = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
@patientId = 1

### Login. Copy the accessToken cookie value from the response into @token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{application}}/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "data": {
    "email": "{{email}}",
    "password": "{{password}}"
  }
}

### Get a patient. Use an existing patient ID.
POST {{baseUrl}}/hospital/patient/mgmt
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: accessToken={{token}}

{
  "type": "get",
  "data": {
    "id": {{patientId}}
  }
}

### Create a patient. This writes a new record.
POST {{baseUrl}}/hospital/patient/mgmt
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: accessToken={{token}}

{
  "type": "create",
  "data": {
    "fullName": "Debug Test Patient",
    "phone": "555-0100"
  }
}

### Update a patient. Replace patientId with an existing test patient ID.
POST {{baseUrl}}/hospital/patient/mgmt
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: accessToken={{token}}

{
  "type": "update",
  "data": {
    "id": {{patientId}},
    "fullName": "Updated Debug Test Patient",
    "phone": "555-0101"
  }
}

### Check an existing patient's existence.
POST {{baseUrl}}/hospital/patient/mgmt
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: accessToken={{token}}

{
  "type": "exists",
  "data": {
    "id": {{patientId}}
  }
}

### Delete is destructive. Replace with a disposable test patient ID.
POST {{baseUrl}}/hospital/patient/mgmt
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: accessToken={{token}}

{
  "type": "delete",
  "data": {
    "id": {{patientId}}
  }
}
